WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:10.019
Imagine this scenario: In 2024, there are
seven candidates for president — a

00:00:10.019 --> 00:00:14.490
Democrat, a Republican, and the nominees
of fringe parties favoring right to life,

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:19.380
choice, gun control, and the green New
Deal... and a billionaire who says he's a

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:23.580
socialist. On election day, the
billionaire gets only 23% of the vote,

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:29.699
but becomes president. "Impossible!" you say,
because no one can win 270 electoral

00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:34.770
votes with only 23% of the popular vote.
But under the National Popular Vote

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:39.360
Compact, an agreement among many states
that their electoral votes will go to

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.170
the candidate who has the most popular
votes, it can happen!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.329
States with 189 electoral votes have
approved the plan, and it goes into

00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:53.940
effect when states with 270 electoral
votes have joined. So a fringe candidate

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:58.050
who gets a small fraction of the total
vote, but still the highest percentage of

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:03.719
the group, will get all 270 electoral
votes of the participating states and

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:06.380
will become president.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.380
Do you think the
winner of the popular vote should become

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:14.600
president, even though he or she only has
a small minority of the popular vote? Let

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:18.119
us know in our poll. Also let us know
what other topics you'd like our

00:01:18.119 --> 00:01:22.680
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be
sure to like and subscribe for more

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.570
research and videos from AEI.

